# What the desktop image's build context leaves behind.
#
# The context is the repository root, because the image ships two files the app
# compiles into itself. Without this, that context is the whole checkout:
# `src-tauri/target` alone is 6.5 GB, `node_modules` another 204 MB, all of it
# read, hashed and handed to the builder before the first instruction runs. On
# Apple Container the builder is a VM, so every byte crosses a virtio mount.
#
# This is BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore file — `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`,
# consulted ahead of any `.dockerignore` at the context root. It is used rather
# than a root one on purpose: `Dockerfile.ci` at the repository root does
# `COPY . .` and needs the whole checkout, and a root ignore file would starve
# it. Apple Container 1.2.2 does read this file — a spike measured the transfer
# drop to 45 B — so the choice is confirmed rather than assumed.
#
# **It must stay an exclude list. No `*`, no `!`.** The first version of this
# file excluded everything and named the six copied files back in with `!`,
# which is the idiom Docker's own documentation uses. Apple Container 1.2.2
# refuses it: the build fails during context transfer with
#
#     #4 ERROR: changes out of order: "computer-image/google-chrome" ""
#
# which names a file that was allowed back in, not the pattern that did it, and
# happens before any instruction runs. `build.sh --check` fails on a `*` or a
# `!` here for that reason.
#
# So: name what stays out, and let everything else through. The cost of that
# form is that a new large directory at the root is in the context until
# somebody adds it here. The cost of the other form was a build that does not
# run at all.

# The repository's own history. Small in a worktree, not in a checkout.
.git
.github

# Session and tooling directories, which in a checkout contain whole worktrees.
.superpowers
.claude

# The frontend: 204 MB of dependencies and the bundle built from them. The
# desktop image is a Linux desktop and has no part of this app in it.
node_modules
dist

# 6.5 GB of build artefacts, and the generated and packaging directories beside
# them. `src-tauri/src` is deliberately absent from this list: the image copies
# `browser.py` and `sessions.py` out of it.
src-tauri/target
src-tauri/gen
src-tauri/icons
src-tauri/capabilities
src-tauri/tests

# Prose, the app's own source, and the scripts that build and spike it. None of
# it is in the image; `build.sh` and `spike-apple.sh` run on the Mac.
docs
src
scripts
